From 87a34f692fe13649ce20de0d948cecb9b7b81884 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: WaleWangPW <396218656@qq.com>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 14:22:59 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 16/22] feat(backend): route managed-root consumers through
 central admission

Task07 routes every destructive managed-root entry through the sealed
central physicaldelete.Admission so the deliberately unavailable executor
denies before any filesystem, Git, or runtime mutation. Consumers gated:
Manager.removeWorktree (RemoveByID / CleanupWorktrees / OnTaskDeleted),
Manager.recreate, Manager.pruneQuarantinedWorktree, workspaces and
tempartifacts Provider.PermanentDelete, GarbageCollector.deleteWorktreeDir,
database.Service.wipeSubdirs (factory reset), and HandoffCleaner
(CleanupPlainFolder / CleanupMultiRepoRoot fallback deletion. Production
wiring reuses the shared physicaldelete.Service on the worktree manager,
task service, handoff cleaner, office GC, factory reset, and both
quarantine providers. Existing tests are updated to the fail-closed
contract; new matrix tests cover every consumer entry and the
nil-admission sentinel. User workspace file edits/deletes remain outside
the managed-root gate.
